    openingText: "You blink awake under a tall white tree, its pale leaves rustling in the morning wind. A handful of villagers kneel nearby, heads bowed. One offers you a bowl of water. Another touches your hair and murmurs, 'The bloom spirit returned…' You're not sure what’s going on, but you’re dry, fed, and surrounded by people who treat you like a sign of hope. Could be worse ways to start over — and the village elder’s already waving you over like you’ve got work to do."
  }
],

  "Truck Impact|World Type: Dark Fantasy World": [
  {
    title: "Given a Job by the Gravekeeper",
    entry: "You woke in a crumbling chapel, face-to-face with a tired old man who assumed you'd been sent to help dig graves.",
    openingText: "You wake on cold stone beneath shattered stained glass, dim light pooling around your legs. A grizzled old man with a rusted shovel peers down at you. 'You one of them sent ones?' he mutters, rubbing a sore shoulder. Before you can speak, he tosses a spare cloak your way. 'Well, you’re breathing. That’ll do. Graves won’t dig themselves.' You follow him outside into a village where everything leans just slightly wrong — and the church bell rings, even though no one pulls the rope."
  },
  {
    title: "Awake in the Ash Garden",
    entry: "You found yourself lying in a ruined garden where nothing grows anymore — only ash, soot, and broken memories.",
    openingText: "You're surrounded by scorched earth and the husks of once-beautiful plants, now reduced to gray stalks. Each step stirs up flakes of white like snowfall in reverse. A single bench remains intact beside a cracked fountain. There’s no sound except the creak of dead branches. Eventually, someone passes by and stares at you. ‘No one's come from that garden in years,’ they say, like you’re a ghost. You’re not sure what this place used to be — but clearly, it’s not forgotten."
  },
  {
    title: "At the Feet of the Forgotten Kings",
    entry: "You woke beneath a row of ancient statues in a ruined plaza. The locals thought the old kings were whispering again — because of you.",
    openingText: "Stone eyes stare blankly above you as you sit up, stiff from the cold. Each statue is weathered and cracked, their names long erased, their swords broken. You hear whispers — not from them, but from the onlookers at the edge of the square. Someone clutches a charm. Another backs away. A child tosses a flower toward your feet, then runs. Apparently, lying here means something to them. You have no idea what. But they’ve started calling you 'the one who woke the stone.'"
  },
  {
    title: "Dragged Out of the River",
    entry: "You were pulled from a half-drowned street by scavengers who thought you'd washed up with the junk. Turns out, you were breathing.",
    openingText: "The first thing you feel is hands grabbing your arm, hauling you out of the thick, grimy water. You cough up mud and river muck onto shattered cobblestones. Around you, crumbling towers lean like drunkards, and a bridge lies half-submerged. 'Thought you were scrap,' someone says, poking your side with a stick. You sit up, dripping, alive — and very much confused. ‘Well, you’re here now,’ another scavenger says, offering stale bread. ‘Hope you’ve got thick skin. This place eats the soft ones.’"
  },
  {
    title: "Found at the Meteor Crater",
    entry: "You landed in a crater near a cursed village, and now they think you're part of the omen that's been brewing for years.",
    openingText: "Smoke curls from the cracked earth as you climb out of a shallow crater, skin still warm from the impact. Around you, people in patched cloaks watch from behind half-collapsed huts. The air smells of sulfur and burned sage. One man steps forward, holding up a bone charm. 'You're the one the crater brought,' he says, grimly. No one smiles. They’re not excited — they’re scared. And judging by the way they start drawing sigils around you, you’re not sure that’s better."
  }
],

  "Truck Impact|World Type: Wild Frontier World": [
  {
    title: "Given a Name by the Clan Elder",
