    openingText: "You sit up, ears ringing. The land around you stretches in all directions — endless grass, bending with the wind. There's no road, no fence, no buildings in sight. Just open sky and the faint sound of hoofbeats far, far away. A few birds circle overhead, then vanish. Whatever brought you here dropped you in the middle of nowhere. Your only clue is a worn satchel on your hip and the simple fact that you're still breathing. Step one: figure out which way not to die."
  },
  {
    title: "Found by the River Tribes",
