    openingText: "You cough up river water onto damp sand. The sky is bright. Figures with furred cloaks and painted faces stand over you, murmuring in a language that sounds like crackling fire and birdcalls. One nudges your boot with a spear, then exchanges glances with the others. 'Not dead,' someone says. 'We keep.' They carry you upriver to a stilted village that smells of fish and herbs. You’re offered soup before questions. The elder just says, 'River chose. We don’t argue with river.'"
  },
