  }
],

  "Truck Impact|World Type: Twilight Fantasy": [
    {
      title: "Before the Waning Oracle",
      entry: "Before your new life began, you stood in a crumbling hall before an ancient Oracle whose visions flickered like dying stars.",
      openingText: "The hall smells of old dust and faded incense. Pillars lean wearily, their carvings half-swallowed by ivy. At its center sits the Oracle — a figure draped in threadbare cloth, their eyes clouded like forgotten moons. They raise a trembling hand toward you, and the space between you quivers as if memory itself strains to reach. You hear no words, only the sigh of a thousand crumbling futures. A slow nod — acceptance or farewell — and the world folds inward, drawing you into its twilight heart."
    },
    {
      title: "Dreaming in the Withered Grove",
      entry: "You awoke beneath the gnarled trees of a dying forest, where petals fall like snow despite no blooms remaining.",
      openingText: "The trees twist toward a colorless sky, branches bare save for drifting, weightless petals that seem to fall from nothing. Beneath your hands, the earth is soft, fed by centuries of forgotten leaves. Somewhere beyond the broken grove, you hear a chime — faint, wavering, lost on the slow breeze. Every breath tastes of cold rain and endings. When you stand, the forest does not stir; it only watches, ancient and still, as if mourning itself."
    },
    {
      title: "Beneath the Last Starfall",
      entry: "You found yourself near the smoking hollow where a star had fallen, its final embers sinking into the waiting earth.",
      openingText: "A shallow crater smolders in the twilight, fringed by scorched grass and glittering stones. The star is long dead, its light a memory clinging stubbornly to the broken soil. Villagers gather at a cautious distance, their heads bowed beneath tattered cloaks stitched with fading constellations. They do not speak. In this world, they say, every fallen star marks another promise the heavens failed to keep. You are left standing alone among the ashes, your shadow long and uncertain."
    },
    {
      title: "Among the Shattered Cloisters",
      entry: "Your first breath in this world was taken among the ruins of a monastery where prayers once soared but now drift like smoke into an empty sky.",
      openingText: "Stone archways frame nothing but broken sky. Vines creep along fallen bells, their mouths forever silent. You rise slowly among shattered mosaics, their glass pieces catching the dying light like fragments of forgotten songs. In the distance, a lone bird calls — a sound almost too small to exist. The cloister's air hums with the ghosts of devotion, a music you feel more than hear, threading through the crumbling bones of a world that remembers it once believed."
    },
    {
      title: "Born of a Fading Dream",
      entry: "The people who found you believe you were woven from the final dreams of a dying god, and treat you with the wary reverence one gives to omens too fragile to touch.",
      openingText: "They approach you with slow, careful steps — figures wrapped in faded cloth, their faces hidden behind cracked masks of sun and moon. They do not ask questions. Instead, they leave small offerings at your feet: a feather, a coin blackened with age, a flower so pale it seems almost made of mist. Around them, the village slouches toward ruin, walls sagging, wells dry. Their eyes hold no hope, only the soft resignation of those who have already said goodbye to the world — and are waiting for you to carry the last whisper forward."
    }
  ],

  "Truck Impact|World Type: High Fantasy World": [
    {
      title: "Before the Aetheric Court",
      entry: "Before your new life began, you stood within a spiraling coliseum of light, summoned before beings whose forms blurred between gods, emperors, and stars.",
      openingText: "Pillars of living crystal rise around you, each one inscribed with languages you cannot even see, much less read. Above, the sky ripples with auroras that pulse like the heartbeat of a sleeping colossus. Figures hover at the far edges of your sight — some armored in flowing banners of flame, others crowned with rings of starlight. Their voices echo not in sound, but in the marrow of your bones, passing judgment beyond mortal understanding. You are seen. You are named. And with a gesture that shatters the sky itself, they cast you into your beginning."
    },
    {
      title: "On the Bridges of Aelthir",
