      entry: "Far above, the constellations themselves shifted, and in their slow, eternal dance, they spoke your name into the waiting world.",
      openingText: "The stars do not fall, nor scream — they simply turn, rearranging themselves into a pattern that has not graced the heavens for a thousand ages. Seers in distant towers stir from their slumber. Oracles clutch at their chests, weeping silent tears. Across the vast world, from sand-choked temples to cities that float like seeds on the breeze, those who watch the skies tremble. They do not yet know who you are — only that a new thread has been woven into the endless tapestry. And you, blinking beneath unfamiliar stars, feel the first slow pull of destiny against your bones."
    }
  ],

