      openingText: "The earth here is dry and pale, grass dead beneath your fingertips. Crooked trees claw at the heavy gray sky, each branch bearing remnants of rough-hewn rope. Beneath one noose, you stir — alone, unclaimed by death. A crow watches you with one cold, yellow eye, then caws once before taking wing. Beyond the hill, the outlines of a fortified town rise from the mist, its walls sharp and unwelcoming. No one will ask where you came from. In this world, asking is dangerous."
