      openingText: "Their camp squats in the shadow of an abandoned watchtower, fires burning low beneath makeshift tarps. Men and women, hard-eyed and hollow-cheeked, sharpen blades and patch worn boots. Their laughter is sharp, edged with desperation. They watch you with suspicion, but they offer food and a place by the fire — for now. Here, honor is currency, trust is a fool’s bet, and survival is a bargain struck anew with every dawn."
    }
  ],

