      openingText: "Tattered banners flutter weakly on rusted poles. The air smells of dry earth and rain that never comes. Summoners kneel where dancers once spun, their hands pressed into broken runes carved long ago. Your arrival stirs no applause, no cheers — only the hollow echo of what might once have been joy."
    }
  ],

  "Failed Summoning Ritual|World Type: Dark Fantasy World": [
  {
    title: "Amid the Ashen Cathedral Choir",
    entry: "You arrived in the desecrated choir pit of a cathedral whose faith had long ago curdled into silence and rot.",
    openingText: "Blackened arches loom overhead, ribs of a sanctum left hollow by betrayal and time. The summoning circle glows faintly amid the cracked stone, its lines smeared by blood and ash. Around you, the pews are splintered, their occupants long turned to bone. Shadows cling unnaturally to the walls, whispering hymns that never end. A cloaked figure kneels before the altar — not in prayer, but in penance — and raises a blade instead of a benediction. You are not a miracle. You are the answer to a question that should never have been asked."
  },
  {
    title: "At the Edge of the Weeping Mire",
    entry: "You manifested half-sunken in a cursed swamp, summoned by desperate exiles who drowned before they could finish the rite.",
    openingText: "Sickly fog coils through the reeds. A crooked stone circle juts from the murk, its runes smeared by rising tide and blood-thick rain. The corpses of the summoners lie nearby, bloated and blind, their mouths still open in final plea. Crows perch on their backs like penance. As you stand, leeches slither from your limbs and vanish into the bog. Something beneath the mire stirs — not angered, not amused — simply waiting."
  },
  {
    title: "Within the Hollow of the Drowned Bell",
    entry: "You awoke inside a cathedral bell long ago torn from its tower and buried beneath centuries of mud and silence.",
    openingText: "The air is tight, wet, and close. Every breath tastes of rust and old prayers. The circle surrounding you glows faintly on the tarnished bronze beneath your feet, pulsing with reluctant memory. Beyond the bell’s curved metal walls, faint wails echo — not speech, not song, but the mourning of stone that remembers being sacred. You were not brought here to save anyone. You were pulled from the dark because someone needed something that would survive it."
  },
  {
    title: "Among the Cracked Graves of the Forgotten Host",
    entry: "You appeared in a graveyard where nameless warriors had once risen in honor — but now lie in twisted, violated rest.",
    openingText: "Moss devours tombstones, and rusted spears jut from the soil like broken fingers. The summoning circle was carved into a mass grave and traced in bone dust, still fresh. As you rise, skeletal hands twitch and reach toward the sky, not to welcome — but to beg. The wind carries no birdsong, only the clatter of teeth gnashing far beneath the ground. Those who summoned you are already gone. The dead, however, remember."
  },
  {
    title: "On the Steps of the Black Monastery",
    entry: "You were summoned before the threshold of a sealed monastery known only in fearful whispers, where none have entered and returned sane.",
    openingText: "The sky bleeds violet light across a barren ridge. The monastery doors stand wide, though no one recalls them ever opening. Summoners in rust-red robes lie in a circle of soot and glass — mouths frozen mid-scream, eyes blind with revelation. A low, resonant hum issues from the dark within. As your foot touches the first step, the doors exhale a breath older than the world, and behind you, the path vanishes."
  }
],

"Failed Summoning Ritual|World Type: High Fantasy World": [
  {
