    openingText: "Time hangs in loops — petals falling, then rising, then falling again. The World-Crystal above you has split into countless floating shards, each reflecting scenes from worlds not yet born. The summoning circle beneath your feet warps as you breathe. Echoes of the spell repeat in chorus from invisible mouths. A single summoner clings to life beside a fountain frozen mid-spill, their voice trapped between joy and madness. This place was never meant to survive your arrival."
  },
  {
    title: "Among the Fallen Choir of Skyreach",
    entry: "You were born in the ruins of a holy sky-temple, its celestial choir obliterated as the summoning backfired.",
    openingText: "White marble columns spiral skyward — cracked and crumbling. Celestial harps lie shattered in the dust, their strings snapped like severed threads of fate. Golden feathers drift across the floor, each one humming softly before turning to ash. The summoning circle glows beneath a fallen archangel, her wings tattered and eyes wide in horror. Her lips move, but no sound comes. You are not the divine answer. You are the echo of their mistake."
  }
],

  "God’s Passing Whim|World Type: Regular Another World Fantasy": [
    {
      title: "In the Celestial Garden",
      entry: "You were chosen within a garden blooming with impossible stars and whispering trees, under the watchful gaze of a goddess of renewal.",
      openingText: "Soft grass cushions your bare feet. Petals made of starlight drift through the air. Before you, a figure in robes of woven dawnlight smiles warmly. 'Another world stirs for you, little seed,' she says, her voice thrumming gently in the marrow of your bones. 'Walk, and see what roots you will grow.' With a faint laugh, she steps aside, and the garden melts into a breath of wind that carries you elsewhere."
    },
    {
