      title: "Within the Hollow Cathedral",
      entry: "You emerged in the ruins of a once-grand cathedral now hollowed of faith, where a god of silence waits.",
      openingText: "Moonlight slithers across broken pews and shattered stained glass. At the altar stands a figure in robes of soot and shadow, no face, no voice, only presence. A single, withered hand lifts toward a door you cannot see — and somehow, you understand. You step forward, and the cold, brittle hush of the world embraces you like a coffin."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Pit of Fallen Crowns",
      entry: "You knelt upon a pit overflowing with broken crowns, before a mocking god of ruin.",
      openingText: "Crowns — dented, rusted, blood-stained — spill into the pit like bones. Leaning against the edge, a lithe figure in tarnished regalia grins down at you. 'They thought they mattered once,' they say, kicking a twisted diadem into the abyss. 'Maybe you'll last longer.' They tap a scepter against your forehead — lightly, mockingly — and the ground crumbles away."
    },
    {
      title: "Before the Well of Ash and Hunger",
      entry: "You stood before a well belching ash and smoke, where a gaunt god of survival judged you with hollow eyes.",
      openingText: "Ash drifts like snow, coating the dead grass underfoot. A figure crouches by the well, gaunt and wrapped in tattered rags. Their voice is a rasp: 'The strong devour the weak. It has always been so.' They toss a coin into the well — and the ash churns upward, swallowing you whole into a world that will test every breath you take."
    }
  ],

  "God’s Passing Whim|World Type: High Fantasy World": [
    {
      title: "At the Argent Steps of Dawn",
      entry: "You stood upon shimmering steps reaching into the sunrise, greeted by a radiant god of beginnings.",
      openingText: "The sky is a canvas of gold and white, each step before you gleaming as if spun from morning light. At the summit, a figure cloaked in woven sunbeams extends a hand. 'Every journey shapes the world,' they intone, voice ringing like a bell across the heavens. As their hand falls, the steps vanish beneath you, and the brilliance becomes another world's sky."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Choir of the First Sky",
      entry: "You emerged amid a celestial choir whose thousand-voiced god called your spirit forward.",
      openingText: "The air thrums with harmony so vast it shakes your bones. Figures of mist and light sing wordless songs, their melodies rising into an endless azure. At the heart of the music, a voice both one and many calls: 'Wake, wanderer. Become another verse.' The sound swells until it lifts you like a leaf into the widening horizon beyond."
    },
    {
      title: "Before the Obsidian Gate of Promised Paths",
      entry: "You stood before a gate carved of night-black stone, guarded by a silent, immutable god.",
      openingText: "The gate towers above you, its surface swirling with constellations yet unborn. A figure robed in velvet darkness watches, offering no words, only the slow drawing aside of one massive hand. The gate shudders open with a sound like falling stars. You step through — and the world behind it claims you as its own."
    },
    {
      title: "Atop the Spire Above Storms",
      entry: "You climbed windswept heights to a storm-forged spire, where a god of storms laughed and beckoned.",
      openingText: "Lightning arcs across a sky blacker than night. Winds buffet the lone spire piercing the clouds. At its peak, a figure crackling with living thunder grins as you approach. 'Brave... or foolish. Both serve,' they shout above the roaring gale. They throw their arms wide — and the storm tears the world open, hurling you downward into destiny."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Verdant Court of the Starborn",
      entry: "You walked among living constellations in a court of endless bloom, greeted by a goddess woven from stars.",
      openingText: "The air glows with petals that hum with starlight. Thrones of crystal and flowering vines line a vast court under a vault of living galaxies. A woman whose skin shimmers with constellations bends low to look at you. 'A fragile thing,' she muses, voice thick with wonder. 'Yet even a single bloom can shift a world.' She smiles — and the court collapses into color, reshaping itself into the land awaiting you."
    }
  ],

  "God’s Passing Whim|World Type: Low Fantasy World": [
    {
      title: "In the Broken Amphitheater",
      entry: "You were summoned to a cracked arena where a weary war-god made no promises of glory.",
      openingText: "Sand stings your skin as the wind howls through the broken arches. A god in dented armor leans heavily on a rusted spear, watching you without much interest. 'Another name for the dirt,' they mutter. 'Go make your mark if you can.' With a shrug, they vanish, and the arena crumbles around you, dropping you into a waiting world."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Crumbling Reliquary",
      entry: "You emerged in a vault of dust-choked relics, acknowledged only in passing by a forgotten goddess.",
      openingText: "Dust hangs thick, muting the gleam of gold and the glint of gems. Amidst the detritus, a woman with cobweb hair lounges, idly flipping through a cracked tome. 'You might outlast the others,' she says, voice dry and brittle. 'Or not.' She waves a skeletal hand — almost lazily — and the vault splits apart, hurling you into the world beyond."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Barren Crossroads",
      entry: "You stood at a featureless crossroads where a laughing wanderer-god pointed the way with a half-hearted grin.",
      openingText: "Dry wind scrapes over cracked stones underfoot. A lanky figure lounges on a crooked milestone, tipping a battered hat your way. 'Left, right, straight ahead...doesn't matter much,' they say with a wink. 'It all ends the same.' A shove between your shoulders propels you stumbling forward, the landscape reshaping itself as you fall into it."
    },
    {
      title: "Before the Worn Throne of Ash",
      entry: "You knelt before a crumbling throne where a hollow-eyed ruler passed their burden without a word.",
      openingText: "Ash sifts down like snow from a dead sky. The throne ahead of you leans precariously, its occupant little more than a shadow wrapped in crumbling robes. They lift one hand — slow, heavy — and the air around you thickens. You are pushed outward, not with malice, but inevitability, and the ashen wind becomes the breath of a new world."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Hollow Plaza",
      entry: "You appeared in a deserted square where no god greeted you — only the lingering echo of faded power.",
      openingText: "Broken statues ring the plaza, their faces worn smooth by time. At the center, a pedestal stands empty, save for the flickering trace of something that might once have been divine. The world does not wait for you. It simply folds you into itself like a sigh — and your journey begins alone."
    }
  ],

  "God’s Passing Whim|World Type: Wild Frontier World": [
    {
      title: "By the Roaring Bonfire at World's Edge",
      entry: "You found yourself before a bonfire that touched the stars, where a spirit of flame and freedom beckoned you onward.",
      openingText: "The fire roars high enough to kiss the swirling clouds. A figure dances within it — wild, laughing, wrapped in sparks and smoke. 'No path but the one you burn yourself,' they shout, voice crackling like dry wood. With a sweep of their arm, the bonfire explodes outward — and the world beyond catches fire in your veins as you tumble into it."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Whispering Stone Circle",
      entry: "You awoke amidst ancient stones that thrummed with the heartbeat of the earth, where a silent god watched.",
      openingText: "Moss clings to the leaning stones, and wind carries voices you almost recognize. At the center, a figure carved from root and bone nods slowly, never speaking. Their hand presses briefly to the earth — and the stones shudder. A path rips open among the grasses and mist, and you are pulled forward into a land still half-dreaming."
    },
    {
      title: "Among the Hanging Roots of the Sky Tree",
      entry: "You dangled from roots that pierced the clouds, laughed at by a god who thrives on upheaval.",
      openingText: "Thick, gnarled roots tangle through the sky, draped with mist and lightning. Perched atop them, a figure swings their legs idly, grinning wide. 'Hope you’re better at landing than flying!' they jeer — and with a playful kick, the root beneath you gives way. You plummet, laughing or screaming, into the waiting wilds below."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Mist-Cloaked Ravine",
      entry: "You found yourself on the lip of a ravine choked with mist, where a god of unseen journeys beckoned.",
      openingText: "The mist coils thick around your ankles, whispering secrets in tongues you almost understand. A shadowy figure stands just out of reach, pointing into the unknown. No words follow — only the creak of old leather and the scent of rain. When you step forward, the ground falls away, and the world catches you in wild, tumbling arms."
    },
    {
      title: "Before the Shattered Horn of the Horizon",
      entry: "You stood at a broken monument overlooking endless wilds, where a god of forsaken beginnings waited.",
      openingText: "The horn, once a beacon, now lies shattered across the stones. A figure wrapped in tattered banners leans against it, gazing into the storm-churned distance. 'No maps. No promises. Just the wind and what you carry,' they say, voice low and rough. They tip an invisible hat — and the horizon swallows you whole."
    }
  ],

  "God’s Passing Whim|World Type: Game-World (Structured Game World)": [
    {
      title: "In the Server Room Beyond Time",
      entry: "You awakened amid tangled cables and endless screens, where a shadowed engineer watched silently.",
      openingText: "Fans hum and screens flicker across walls that seem to stretch forever. A figure in a stained hoodie leans back in a cracked chair, lifting a coffee cup in silent salute. 'Huh. Didn't expect you so soon,' they mutter. They tap a console lazily, and the code around you folds inward — shoving you into the game-space like a file sent by accident."
    },
    {
      title: "On the Control Deck of the First Instance",
      entry: "You were briefed by a VR architect in a gleaming observation deck suspended above cascading data streams.",
      openingText: "Polished steel gleams under your feet. Beneath the transparent floor, rivers of luminous code rush by like waterfalls. A sharply dressed figure adjusts holographic schematics midair. 'You’ll be fine... probably,' they say, not looking at you. A casual flick of their wrist — and gravity drops away, casting you into the initialization sequence of a new world."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Fractured Tutorial Chamber",
      entry: "You woke amid the fractured remnants of a training room, where glitches drifted like broken dreams.",
      openingText: "Polygons jitter at the edges of vision. Tutorial prompts flicker and vanish mid-sentence. A disembodied voice buzzes in your ears: 'W-elcome, p-p-player. Initializa-tion comp-lete. Good...l-uck?' The floor tilts like a broken disk, and you tumble forward — into a world where rules half-work and reality strains at the seams."
    },
    {
      title: "Inside the Admin Sanctum",
      entry: "You stood in a sterile white space where an indifferent system AI reviewed your existence with clinical disinterest.",
      openingText: "Lines of floating data scroll endlessly along glowing walls. At the center hovers a sphere of light, pulsing once with each of your heartbeats. A cold voice intones: 'Candidate accepted. Deployment imminent.' A doorway of static opens before you — and something unseen shoves you bodily through it."
    },
    {
      title: "In the Memory Echo Lobby",
      entry: "You found yourself in a half-forgotten lobby where old system messages and player memories flickered like ghosts.",
      openingText: "Benches line the empty space, and flickering holograms replay scenes you cannot quite place. Voices echo: 'Patch 1.3... Logout error... Player deleted...' No one speaks to you — but the lobby dissolves like a wiped hard drive, leaving only a final blinking prompt: ENTER WORLD >. You fall forward through it without touching a key."
    }
  ],

  "God’s Passing Whim|World Type: Game-World (Game Turned Reality)": [
    {
      title: "In the Collapsing Debug Room",
      entry: "You awoke amid flickering error codes, as a desperate fragment of an AI urged you onward.",
      openingText: "The world pixelates and warps. Red warnings scream across the air itself. A jagged figure, its body half-light, half-code, points urgently to a breach in the fracturing walls. 'Run...run...run...' it stutters, glitching through five different voices. The floor disintegrates beneath your feet before you can even answer."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Abandoned Dev Terminal",
      entry: "You stumbled into a forgotten dev console, where the last message from a vanished creator blinked quietly.",
      openingText: "Dust swirls in the static-frozen air. A terminal whirs weakly, projecting a cracked, looping message: 'If anyone... can still see this...I'm sorry.' The words distort, stretch, then collapse. A door made of pure white noise flickers open — and pulls you through before you can second-guess."
    },
    {
      title: "Before the Glitched Council of Avatars",
      entry: "You stood before corrupted echoes of old game characters, who ushered you forward with hollow ceremony.",
      openingText: "They stand arrayed in broken armor, faces shimmering between identities. One steps forward — a knight, a scholar, a merchant — shifting uncontrollably. 'Hero...villain...visitor...' the chorus intones, overlapping and out of sync. Their glitching hands push open a cracked portal, and you stumble into a reality no longer bound by clean code."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Graveyard of Forgotten Patches",
      entry: "You wandered into ruins where failed updates lie abandoned like broken prayers.",
      openingText: "Crumbling structures wear labels: 'Patch 2.0,' 'Emergency Hotfix,' 'Rollback Save.' The air is thick with memory — broken quests, half-finished NPCs, rusted artifacts of intention. In the distance, a static storm brews. When the ground beneath you crumbles, you fall willingly — for anything must be better than standing still."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Null Gateway",
      entry: "You faced a formless gateway where corrupted systems whispered conflicting promises.",
      openingText: "Nothingness yawns before you — not darkness, not light, but absence. Shapes ripple through it: fragments of lost servers, discarded avatars, system errors howling like wind. Somewhere in the emptiness, a cracked voice murmurs: 'Proceed...or be forgotten.' You step forward — not because you trust, but because the alternative is worse."
    }
  ],

  "God’s Passing Whim|World Type: Endless Winter World": [
    {
      title: "Before the Icebound Throne",
      entry: "You stood before a throne carved from ancient glacial stone, where a king of endless frost weighed your worth in silence.",
      openingText: "The air freezes in your throat. Seated atop a throne that groans under its own weight, a figure swathed in furs and frost leans forward slightly, studying you with eyes the color of distant stars. He says nothing. Only raises a hand, and the world fractures — plunging you into the endless cold."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Last Hearth Under the Stars",
      entry: "You found yourself by the last living fire beneath a sky of unmoving constellations, tended by a goddess of stubborn hope.",
      openingText: "A single hearth burns in defiance against the night. Beside it stands a woman cloaked in a thousand patchwork prayers, her hand shielding the flame. She looks at you — not smiling, not speaking — and nods once. The fire flares blindingly — and when your vision clears, the hearth is gone, and a frozen world stretches before you."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Frostbitten Archway",
      entry: "You passed beneath a crumbling archway where a silent, frozen spirit watched with hollow patience.",
      openingText: "The stones sag under the weight of endless ice. A shape, neither wholly human nor wholly wind, lingers beside the archway, frost clinging to its transparent form. It lifts a single hand in farewell — and as you cross the threshold, the ice grips your limbs, pulling you across into the breathless hush of another world."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Silent Huntress’ Grove",
      entry: "You wandered into a grove of skeletal trees where a goddess of the winter wilds waited in perfect silence.",
      openingText: "The trees, black and bare, rise like pleading arms into a bruised sky. At their center crouches a woman wrapped in animal skins and shadow, one hand resting on the hilt of a bone bow. She meets your gaze, and without a word, turns her back. A path tears open behind her — a path you have no choice but to follow."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Glacier’s Hollow Heart",
      entry: "You awoke within a cavern of living ice, where a buried ancient voice whispered once, then fell silent forever.",
      openingText: "The ice walls pulse faintly with blue light, casting your reflection a thousand times over. From deep within the glacier, a voice as old as the world murmurs a single word — a name, perhaps, or a farewell. The ground beneath you groans and cracks, and the frozen heart of the world spits you out into its endless, glittering desolation."
    }
  ],

  "God’s Passing Whim|World Type: Twilight World": [
    {
      title: "In the Echoing Chapel of Lost Names",
      entry: "You stood within a hollow chapel where a whispering god barely remembered the reason for your summoning.",
      openingText: "Broken pews and shattered stained glass litter the floor. The air is thick with dust and the scent of rain long past. From the altar, a faint, wavering voice calls: 'Another soul... another chance... or was it penance?' The words drift apart like smoke, and the world outside the chapel reshapes itself around your arrival."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Cracked Observatory",
      entry: "You gazed through a broken lens beside a fading god who could no longer name the constellations.",
      openingText: "The great brass telescope is shattered, pointing toward a sky with fewer stars each night. A robed figure leans on it like a crutch, tracing vanished constellations with a trembling hand. 'We used to know their names...' they murmur, almost to themselves. A falling star — or a fragment of memory — streaks past, pulling you along with it into another world."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Drowned Bell Tower",
      entry: "You awoke within a flooded tower where the bell’s toll could no longer reach heaven.",
      openingText: "Water laps at crumbling stones, carrying fragments of forgotten prayers. A spectral figure tugs once at a rope covered in moss, trying — and failing — to ring the drowned bell. They glance at you, hollow-eyed, then turn away. A current unseen catches your body — and drags you down into the deeper places of this fading world."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Garden of Withering Dreams",
      entry: "You passed through a garden of dead flowers where a god of forgotten hopes set you adrift.",
      openingText: "Colorless petals drift through the air like ashes. Vines coil around broken marble statues. A figure kneels in the dead soil, their hands gently cupping a single wilting bloom. They lift their gaze to you — ancient, sorrowful — and simply nod. The garden dissolves around you like mist, and the weight of a world nearing its end presses on your skin."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Last Hall of the Silent Court",
      entry: "You stood in a ruined court where the shades of gods once judged greatness — now they barely notice you.",
      openingText: "Cracked thrones line the crumbling hall. Figures of mist sit atop them, staring into the distance with empty eyes. No fanfare greets your arrival; no sentence is passed. One by one, they turn away — and the heavy doors behind you creak open into a world that has already begun to forget itself."
    }
  ],

  "Dream Rebirth|World Type: Regular Another World Fantasy": [
    {
      title: "Waking in the Misty Glade",
      entry: "You awoke alone in a mist-laden glade, unfamiliar stars fading overhead.",
      openingText: "The grass is damp beneath your fingers. A sword and a traveler's cloak lie nearby, as if you placed them down yourself. Mist swirls low, carrying the scent of rain and pine. Distantly, you hear a stream gurgling — and somewhere beyond that, the low howl of something waking up with you."
    },
    {
      title: "Living Another’s Life in the Peasant's Cottage",
      entry: "You awoke in a humble cottage, called by a name you didn't recognize.",
      openingText: "The rough wool blanket itches against your skin. The smell of bread and woodsmoke fills the single-room cottage. An old woman smiles warmly at you from a small hearth. 'Up late again, Leren,' she says, affection in her voice. You blink — the name does not fit your mouth, but the world accepts it without question."
    },
    {
      title: "Journeying in Another’s Place on the Merchant's Wagon",
      entry: "You awoke amidst jostling sacks and creaking wood, treated as a traveling apprentice.",
      openingText: "The wagon rocks with each rut and stone. A man with a wide hat calls over his shoulder, 'Keep those crates tied down, lad!' His voice is gruff but not unkind. Your hands, stained with ink and rope burns, move on instinct — though you cannot recall ever learning these trades."
    },
    {
      title: "Beneath the Festival Tree",
      entry: "You woke under a giant tree adorned with lanterns, amid a sleeping village festival.",
      openingText: "The branches above are strung with hundreds of glowing paper lanterns, swaying gently. Around you, villagers sleep where they fell — laughter still faint on their breath. The smell of honeyed bread and mead lingers. Somewhere in the distance, a flute plays a lonely, wavering note."
    },
    {
      title: "In the Ruins of the Watchtower",
      entry: "You found yourself within the crumbling remains of a forgotten watchtower at dawn.",
      openingText: "Cracked stones press cool against your back. The roof has long since fallen in, letting a weak, golden sun brush the ruined floor. Wildflowers have claimed the cracks, and in the distance, the faint shapes of villages and forests stretch into the mist. A path leads downward — where it goes, you do not know."
    }
  ],

  "Dream Rebirth|World Type: Post-Post Apocalypse Fantasy": [
    {
      title: "Among the Sunken Meadows",
      entry: "You awoke in a meadow where vines devoured the bones of ancient towers.",
      openingText: "The air hums with unseen magic. Around you, broken teeth of skyscrapers jut from the earth, wrapped in centuries of moss and flowering ivy. Birds the color of molten gold flutter between rusted beams. In the distance, thunder murmurs across a sky stitched with green auroras."
    },
    {
      title: "Living Another’s Life in the Sage’s Hut",
      entry: "You awoke in a stone hut, in the simple life of an apprentice to a forgotten way.",
      openingText: "The fire crackles low in the pit. Shelves of strange, bone-bound tomes line the rough walls. A gnarled old man snores on a cot nearby. By the door, a staff leans — one you recognize but cannot name. A worn tunic clings to your skin, the fabric stamped with a sigil you should not know."
    },
    {
      title: "Hunting in Another’s Skin in the Broken Wilds",
      entry: "You awoke mid-hunt, fingers taut on a bow crafted from bone and spiritwood.",
      openingText: "The brush crackles as something vast stirs nearby. Your feet, bare and calloused, find silent footing on the moss. Tattoos wind up your arms — symbols of a life you never lived. A breathless voice murmurs behind your teeth: *Aim. Loose. Survive.* You obey without understanding why."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Petrified Forest’s Edge",
      entry: "You awoke beneath massive stone trees where a city once stood proud.",
      openingText: "Colossal trunks of fused metal and fossilized wood loom overhead, their roots splitting ancient roads. The wind moans through hollow ruins, carrying the scent of salt and forgotten prayers. When you move, the ground shifts — and somewhere, something begins to wake with you."
    },
    {
      title: "Beside the Black River of Spires",
      entry: "You found yourself at the banks of a river whose waters reflected broken memories.",
      openingText: "The river runs thick and black, glittering like oil under a pale sun. Rusted metal spires rise from the water like skeletal hands. Strange ripples disturb the surface, though no wind blows. Your reflection shivers — and for a moment, shows a face you do not yet remember wearing."
    }
  ],

  "Dream Rebirth|World Type: Dark Fantasy World": [
    {
      title: "On the Bloodied Battlefield",
      entry: "You awoke among corpses and broken spears, beneath a sky heavy with smoke.",
      openingText: "The metallic stench of blood chokes the air. Ravens croak from ruined standards jutting from the mud. Your armor — battered, ill-fitting — is stained with battles you do not remember. Far across the fields, the horns of scavengers sound. You are not alone for long."
    },
    {
      title: "Living Another’s Life in the Thief’s Den",
      entry: "You awoke in a filthy cellar where hardened thieves called you brother.",
      openingText: "The floorboards creak above as heavy boots stomp by. Around you, battered crates and smuggled goods are stacked like crude furniture. Someone shoves a sack into your hands: 'Your turn to run it, Riv.' You don't know the name — but the dagger at your belt feels familiar enough."
    },
    {
      title: "Brawling in Another’s Place at the Tavern",
      entry: "You awoke mid-brawl, fists swinging and tankards flying through a smoky tavern.",
      openingText: "A blow catches your jaw, sending you sprawling across a sticky, sawdust-strewn floor. All around, bodies crash into tables, laughter and curses blending into a single drunken roar. A woman shoves a mug into your hand with a wink. 'Get up, fool — you're winning!' she shouts, just before a chair splinters nearby."
    },
    {
      title: "Among the Plague-Ravaged Village",
      entry: "You awoke in the heart of a dying village, where silence carried heavier than any prayer.",
      openingText: "The houses sag under the weight of decay. Tattered ribbons hang from doorways, warnings for all to stay away. Crows pick at abandoned carts. A child's doll floats face down in a muddy puddle. In the distance, a single cracked bell tolls — but no one answers it anymore."
    },
    {
      title: "Within the Half-Collapsed Church",
      entry: "You found yourself among the ruined pews of a forgotten church, cold candles still flickering.",
      openingText: "Half the ceiling lies in shattered ruin, open to the grey, pitiless sky. Broken stained glass glitters in the rubble. Candles gutter in cracked holders, their flames stubborn against the growing wind. A holy symbol, long tarnished, rests heavy around your neck — a memory of a faith you never chose."
    }
  ],

  "Dream Rebirth|World Type: High Fantasy World": [
    {
      title: "On the Drifting Sky-Isle",
      entry: "You awoke atop a fragment of land adrift among the clouds, untethered and free.",
      openingText: "The sky is endless and blinding blue. Around you, fragments of ancient ruins float lazily on unseen currents. Birds with sapphire feathers cry out as they wheel past. A silver bridge stretches between isles — impossibly thin, impossibly strong — and somewhere beyond it, a city gleams like a second sun."
    },
    {
      title: "Living Another’s Life in the Noble’s Chamber",
      entry: "You awoke wrapped in silk and sunlight, cradled by a life of privilege.",
      openingText: "Gossamer curtains sway with the morning breeze. Robed servants move quietly through the chamber, arranging breakfast and polished armor. One bows low. 'My lord — your coronation awaits.' You rise instinctively, muscles unused to the burden of expectation already aching under invisible crowns."
    },
    {
      title: "Dueling in Another’s Skin at the Wizard Academy",
      entry: "You awoke mid-incantation, facing a furious opponent across a courtyard of rune-carved stones.",
      openingText: "The air crackles with unfinished spells. A woman in gold-stitched robes snarls a challenge, sigils blooming around her fingertips. Around you, students chant and cheer, watching the duel unfold. Your own hands raise — shaped by training you do not remember — and power hums at your fingertips, eager to answer."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Roots of the World-Tree",
      entry: "You found yourself beneath a world-tree whose roots carved valleys and whose leaves caught stars.",
      openingText: "The tree's trunk rises beyond sight, its bark a tapestry of shifting glyphs. Streams of luminous mist spiral down from the branches, feeding the earth. Creatures of dream and starlight drink from silver pools. In your hand, a seed pulses with quiet power — placed there by someone you can no longer name."
    },
    {
      title: "At the Gates of the Crystal City",
      entry: "You awoke before a city spun from light and crystal, where songs shaped the very stones.",
      openingText: "Great spires rise, catching the dawn and fracturing it into rivers of color. Bridges of music carry travelers between towers. A herald in iridescent armor approaches, bowing deeply. 'The City of Arakhel welcomes you, Dreamer.' Behind him, gates of pure song shimmer open — and destiny hums just beyond."
    }
  ],

  "Dream Rebirth|World Type: Low Fantasy World": [
    {
      title: "In the Rain-Soaked Field",
      entry: "You awoke in a cold, muddy field under iron-grey skies.",
      openingText: "Rain beats against your skin in relentless sheets. Around you, broken wagon wheels and scattered weapons hint at some lost skirmish. No banners fly, no voices call. Only the low moan of the wind answers. You rise, soaked and shivering, without memory — and without a friend in sight."
    },
    {
      title: "Living Another’s Life in the Tavern's Back Room",
      entry: "You awoke behind the cracked walls of a grimy tavern, already owing more than you could repay.",
      openingText: "The smell of sour ale and burnt bread clings to your roughspun clothes. Heavy footsteps pass outside the thin door, and a gruff voice calls: 'Shift starts at first bell, brat.' Your hands are calloused — your pockets empty. Somehow, this world expects you to already belong."
    },
    {
      title: "Brawling in Another’s Skin in the Market",
      entry: "You awoke mid-fight, your fingers still clenched around a stranger’s stolen coin.",
      openingText: "Shouts rise around you. Rough hands grab your cloak, and a punch glances off your jaw. Stalls topple; apples roll underfoot. A bearded man curses your name — a name you don't yet know. Instinct pulls you sideways, ducking beneath a swinging cudgel. Survival is the only language spoken here."
    },
