    }
  ],

  "Teleportation Malfunction|World Type: Regular Another World Fantasy": [
    {
      title: "The Doorway in the Weeping Woods",
      entry: "The elevator faded into a rotting wooden door set into a massive oak.",
      openingText: "Mist coils low across tangled roots as you stumble out. The air is thick with the scent of moss and damp earth. Behind you, the elevator groans — and as you glance back, it is simply a battered wooden door half-swallowed by the tree. Around you, towering forests stretch to an endless horizon, their ancient trunks whispering secrets in a language you almost understand."
    },
    {
      title: "The Vanishing Door of Crowhaven",
      entry: "The elevator dissolved, leaving you on a cobblestone street in a forgotten town.",
      openingText: "Gas lamps gutter in the fog, casting wavering shadows across abandoned houses. You whirl around — but the elevator is gone, replaced by cracked stones underfoot. Somewhere distant, a church bell tolls. The streets twist like a maze, and something unseen watches from behind shuttered windows."
    },
    {
      title: "The Fallen Gate of Serathwyn",
      entry: "The elevator became a broken stone arch near crumbling ruins.",
      openingText: "The air smells of old rain and forgotten battles. Vines strangle shattered statues and walls long surrendered to the wild. The arch behind you, once grand, now crumbles stone by stone until only memory remains. Beyond the ruins, faint campfires flicker — civilization's fragile flickers against the swallowing night."
    },
    {
      title: "The Fading Portal in the Green Hollow",
      entry: "The elevator warped into a circle of standing stones in a hidden glen.",
      openingText: "Flowers you cannot name bloom in profusion, their scents dizzying. The stones hum softly, but the resonance fades as you watch — soon they are only cold, cracked monuments. A river sings nearby, and in the distance, a village of thatched roofs nestles under the towering trees."
    },
    {
      title: "The Shifting Pathway of Braemarch",
      entry: "The elevator was replaced by a rough trail at the edge of a misty valley.",
      openingText: "The mountains loom like sleeping giants. The trail twists into mist and mystery, and the distant cries of strange beasts echo faintly. You feel an invisible push — as if the land itself urges you forward. The way back is gone. Only the endless road remains."
    }
  ],

  "Teleportation Malfunction|World Type: Post-Post Apocalypse Fantasy": [
